node_modules
.remotion
*.log

# The rendered cuts are kept rather than ignored. They are what a judge or a
# reader is actually looking for, they are about twelve megabytes in total,
# and a submission that depends on a hosting link staying up is a submission
# with a part that can quietly stop working.
#
# The check stills are not kept: they are scratch output from verifying a
# composition, and they are regenerated by `remotion still` whenever needed.
out/check-*.png

# Nor are the source stills. They are twelve megabytes of derived data that
# `npm run frames` reproduces exactly — the scene is painted from a fixed
# sequence — so carrying them would be storing the output of a command next
# to the command.
public/frames
